# Does a god-marked item worn in the HELMET slot work as a holy symbol?
# Read by tools/check_holy_symbol_slots.sh, bead inc-tf6l.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/holy-symbol-slot.keys 1
#
# A priest of Aiswin, built by @include chargen-priest.keys. The session must
# run against the SCRATCH module the check builds (lib/ plus
# tools/fixtures/holy-symbol-slot-helm.irh appended), never the shipped one:
# that fixture adds a helmet whose effect is named "Aiswin Test Helm", which is
# the god mark the code's own prefix test reads. See the check's header.
#
# THE STEPS, and why each is here.
#
#   ESC                      chargen-priest ends with the four starting spells
#                            and leaves a "Select direction, location or
#                            target:" prompt open; ESC answers it. (Same first
#                            key as tools/keys/divine-feat-gear.keys.)
#
#   i                        the inventory manager. The priest starts with his
#   o SPACE s                holy symbol WORN in the Neck slot (races.irh's
#                            EV_BIRTH wields it there via Character::GainItem's
#                            prefslot). If it stays on, turning works through
#                            the old amulet slot whatever the fix does. Take it
#                            off: 'o' selects Neck, SPACE lifts the symbol into
#                            the air, 's' stows it in the pack, ESC leaves.
#
#   w y                      wizard mode, then its options menu. 'w' is the
#                            wizard key and 'y' answers the enable prompt.
#
#   Item Acquisition         the acquisition browser.
#   RIGHT*18                 walk the glyph row to Helms. ItemGlyphs
#                            (src/Tables.cpp:339-340) puts -AI_HELM 18 steps
#                            along, and the header line names the category, so a
#                            miscount shows as another word after the colon.
#   @until "Aiswin Test      the candidate list has no menu letters, so the
#     Helm" DOWN             cursor is walked. @until stops on the pass where
#                            the wanted name first appears at the bottom of the
#                            three-row window; one further DOWN moves the
#                            highlight onto it.
#   @expect "Aiswin Test     nail the name to the row before taking it, so a
#     Helm"                  drifted cursor stops the run here instead of
#                            quietly taking the neighbour.
#   ENTER                    take it; it lands in the 'In the Air' slot and the
#                            inventory manager opens.
#   q SPACE                  'q' selects the Helmet slot and SPACE swaps the helm
#                            onto the head. ESC leaves the manager.
#   @dump:helm-worn          the helm is on the head and the Neck slot is empty.
#
#   @until "Use which skill" u   the Use menu; @choose "Turn Undead" takes it.
#   @dump:turn-worn          THE RED/GREEN READING. After the fix the god-marked
#                            helm in the helmet slot qualifies, so the game
#                            prints "You channel the sacred energies of Aiswin.
#                            Nothing happens." Before the fix the four-slot
#                            search misses the helmet and the game prints "You
#                            need an appropriate Holy Symbol to affect undead."
#
#   i                        take the helm back off into the pack:
#   q SPACE s                'q' selects Helmet, SPACE lifts the helm into the
#                            air, 's' stows it. ESC leaves. This is the CONTROL.
#   @dump:helm-stowed        the helmet slot is empty again.
#   @dump:turn-pack          turning is refused with the helm in the pack, on
#                            both builds -- the pack is not a worn slot.

@include chargen-priest.keys

ESC

i
o SPACE s
@dump:symbol-stowed
ESC

w
y
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*18
@until "Aiswin Test Helm" DOWN
@expect "Aiswin Test Helm"
DOWN
ENTER
q SPACE
@dump:helm-worn
ESC

@until "Use which skill" u
@choose "Turn Undead"
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:turn-worn

@until "Things in View" ESC
i
q SPACE s
@dump:helm-stowed
ESC

@until "Use which skill" u
@choose "Turn Undead"
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:turn-pack
@quit
